Z||000006||count_iblis||11-10-2000||11:06 AM||||Guys, I have seen two lawyers and they have both said the same thing.  Here in KY lemon laws only work with new cars, or cars under a warranty.  The car I bought was a AS IS, WHERE IS.  Meaning that once i signed the papers and all it was my problem.  The lawyer's said the only thing I can do is go to the court house and take sign up for a samll claims court. Thats about it.  But the guy that sold it to me is actually been pretty cool this friday morning.  He said after the garage I took it to looks at it, he wants me to bring it back up there and he said he would see what he can do.  So at this point I have several options.  I will keep you guys posted. Im going to keep the car no matter what, I already have an attachment to it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>COUNTIBLIS <BR>"HUG YOUR KIDS SPANK THE SOUND BARRIER"||||reg||1
