Z||000024||fropuff||11-11-2000||12:09 AM||||That's too bad about the whole deal.  That also sucks that you don't have lemon laws.  Here in Minnesota, there is a 30 day? warranty for new cars; 3 for cars w/o a warranty.  My cousin works at an oil change place, and this lady brought in her 97 Blazer.  They pulled the plug, and they noticed a grease coming out.  It turns out it was Vasaline.  The dealer put it in there to get rid of a knock.  She got it changed 4 days after she got it, without a warranty, so she was screwed.  I hope your 3.1/3.4 turns out; that's a good idea to do anyway; it's just too bad you had to do it so soon.  Sorry.||||reg||1
