Z||000028||DavidHenshaw||11-11-2000||04:09 PM||||Ok, you've talked to two lawyers and they say you're up the creek. Now is the time to contact Kentucky State Consumer Protection and Consumer Protection for your local area. I'm not saying these two lawyers don't know what they are talking about, I'm just saying be sure before you accept their advice.<P>It wouldn't be the first time 2 lawyers were wrong on the same subject. Also its hard to believe Ky would be so far behind the rest of the country on consumer pretection. Good luck.<P>Dave<P>86 GT <P>||||reg||1
Z||000029||chicagoGT||11-13-2000||12:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by count_iblis:<BR><B>Philphine,<P>Which guy did you speak with?  Was he a younger guy or older guy?  I talked to Marvin the sales mngr.  He was a real Di*K.  I almost didnt come back but he called me back and asked if I was comming back up to buy it.<P>Count iblis,<P>If Marvin boy wants to be a pr*ck about the whole thing may i suggest that you take some yellow paint that washes off with water and wont harm your car and paint lemons all over the car with a large sign in the front and rear windows telling the world how he stuck it to you. Then legally park your car in front of his lot. He may be willing to deal( total refund or partial ) and if not, revenge is one of lifes sweeter statisfactions when dealing with people like this.  p.s. friend of my did this and after a week got his money back<P>GOOD LUCK   <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||3
